{
  "requirement": "`habeas setup` MUST configure native nextest settings in\n`.config/nextest.toml` at the Cargo workspace root so the coverage workflow of\n{cite}`requirements.test-coverage.run` routes each executed test attempt through\nthe per-process collector of {cite}`requirements.test-coverage.processes`.\nThose settings MUST use nextest's own configuration format.\nRepeating setup MUST avoid duplicate configuration, preserve unrelated nextest\nsettings, and report conflicting settings for review rather than overwrite them.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately cover `requirements.test-coverage.setup.configuration`. I read `configure`, `check`, `validate_setup` and `workspace_root` in `src/execution_coverage/configuration.rs`. I used them only to see what the tests' inputs and assertions exercise.\n\n**Obligations and the tests that cover them**\n\n1. **Setup writes native nextest settings to `.config/nextest.toml` at the Cargo workspace root.**\n   - `mod[tests]/fn[workspace_member_uses_the_native_config_at_the_workspace_root]` runs `configure` from a member crate. It asserts the path is the workspace root's `.config/nextest.toml` and that the member has no `.config` directory. It then checks the excluded-member case, where the member is its own root.\n   - `mod[tests]/fn[explicit_workspace_pointer_places_configuration_at_a_sibling_workspace]` does the same for a `workspace = '../workspace'` pointer.\n   - `tests/setup.rs#fn[coverage_setup_is_idempotent_and_hook_needs_no_coverage_chapter]` runs the real `habeas setup` and asserts `.config/nextest.toml` exists and contains `coverage-process`.\n\n2. **The settings route every executed attempt through the per-process collector.**\n   - The generated source is passed to `check`, which requires the following. The check is asserted to pass for the default profile, for `ci`, and for inherited profiles.\n     - A `wrapper-scripts` experimental feature.\n     - A `scripts.wrapper.habeas-coverage` entry that runs `habeas coverage-process` with `target-runner = \"within-wrapper\"`.\n     - An unconditional `all()` `run-wrapper` rule.\n   - `fn[native_settings_inheritance_and_precedence]` asserts rejection of the following. Together these show the settings must really route all attempts, not merely mention the collector.\n     - A wrong command.\n     - A wrong target-runner.\n     - A filtered rule.\n     - A platform-conditioned rule.\n     - A conflicting inherited rule.\n     - An inheritance cycle.\n   - It also asserts that a child profile can override the conflict.\n\n3. **The settings use nextest's own format.** The tests parse and validate TOML with the native keys (`experimental`, `scripts.wrapper`, `profile.*.scripts`, `run-wrapper`, `inherits`), and `check` is run on the output.\n\n4. **Repeating setup avoids duplicates.**\n   - `fn[native_settings_inheritance_and_precedence]` asserts that `configure` on its own output equals the source.\n   - The integration test runs `habeas setup` twice and asserts the config file is byte-identical.\n\n5. **Setup preserves unrelated settings.** `fn[native_settings_inheritance_and_precedence]` starts from a file with `experimental = ['setup-scripts']`, `retries = 2` and a `setup = 'prepare'` rule. It asserts all three survive in the output of `configure`.\n\n6. **Setup reports conflicts rather than overwriting them.**\n   - `fn[setup_conflicts_name_the_setting_and_preserve_existing_native_configuration]` covers these conflicts:\n     - A wrong wrapper command.\n     - A wrong `target-runner`.\n     - `experimental` of the wrong type.\n     - `scripts` of the wrong type.\n     - `profile.default.scripts` of the wrong type.\n     - A conflicting run-wrapper rule.\n\n     For each one it asserts the error names the setting and `.config/nextest.toml`, and that the file on disk is unchanged.\n   - `tests/setup.rs#fn[setup_reports_a_conflicting_nextest_wrapper_without_writing_project_files]` covers the CLI. The command fails, stderr names the file and the setting, and the config and the other project files are untouched.\n   - The idempotency test also shows the SessionStart hook advises setup on a conflicting config without modifying it.\n\n**Gaps and exemptions**\n\nI found no gaps. The cited requirements `requirements.test-coverage.run` and `requirements.test-coverage.processes` are context only. I did not reassess their implementation or tests. No `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "96b720306e7c96652a5898cfb92a56832cb17c63aaeae24e722eaab32c461e25",
